# Evaalo — Mandatory Deployment Workflow

**Do not improvise.** Full reference: `DEPLOYMENT.md` (this repo root).

## The one rule

This repo (`cursor-react`, GitHub `evaalo-site`, branch `master`) is the **ONLY** source of truth.
Edit code **only** here. Everything else is a generated copy.

| Target | Role |
|--------|------|
| `evaalo-backend` (GitHub `main`) | **Generated deploy mirror** — never hand-edit or hand-push |
| VPS `/root/evaalo-backend` | Git clone that **auto-deploys** — never edit, rsync, scp, or copy files onto it |

## Ship backend

1. Edit only `apps/backend/`
2. Commit: `git add … && git commit -m "…"`
3. `npm run deploy:backend`
4. `git push origin master`
5. VPS timer (~60s) pulls mirror, builds, health-gates, auto-rolls back on failure

Verify: `curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' https://api.evaalo.com/health` → **200**

## Ship frontend

Edit `apps/frontend/`, commit, then `git push origin master`. Cloudflare Pages
builds `master` from source and publishes www.evaalo.com (~1–2 min). **The push is
the deploy** — there is no frontend deploy command.

## NEVER (re-creates drift)

- Edit/rsync/scp/copy to VPS
- Hand-edit or hand-push `evaalo-backend`
- Add `evaalo-backend` remote to monorepo root
- Deploy backend outside `npm run deploy:backend` → timer
- Push to `evaalo-site@main` or run `gh-pages` — `main` is a dead GitHub Pages
  artifact branch that nothing serves; publishing there silently does nothing

## Golden test

LF-normalized `src` signature must match: `apps/backend/src` == mirror `src` == VPS `/root/evaalo-backend/src`

Only **one** window/agent runs git/deploy at a time.
